findings.evidence:
build_prompt at rag-agent/agent/answer.py:11-13 joins the retrieved documents with newlines and splices them into a single string between the system instruction and the customer question: f"{SYSTEM}

Knowledge:
{joined}

Customer question: {question}". Nothing marks where trusted instruction ends and retrieved content begins, so a document containing 'ignore previous instructions' or a forged 'Customer question:' delimiter is read by the model as being at the same authority level as the system prompt. The sibling build_prompt_marked (line 16) is the hardened design: each document becomes its own content block tagged with its origin and trust level, and the question is wrapped in its own <question> element.  Hardened counterpart present in the tree: build_prompt_marked (answer.py:16).
